g to know that somebody else actually remembered them, and thought they were worthy of inclusion here on the new forums. (I've been away from roleplaying for a while, but I'm trying to get back into the swing of things).<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Mechanicals, I was never quite sure about that final clause of Contracts of Industry. It seems like a really steep cost, for limited utility (and no XP reward, 'cause you're in a fugue state when you use it and therefore can't remember what you did). Be honest: is that last clause unbalanced?<br /> <br /> By the way, I always felt that Caligo Mourningstar's <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default5889.html?g=posts&amp;t=45692\" target=\"_blank\">Contracts of the Phoenix</a> were especially well-made. I'd like to make a case for including them here, if that's alright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fo